{
  "_hinweis": "Templates for the Duopilo ATC. Best make your own changes in a copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Duopilo\\atc-templates.json – it takes precedence and is not overwritten by updates. Then run atc_control reload. Variables are written in {braces}; with several variants, the first one whose variables are all known wins. Duopilo speaks numbers digit by digit, speeds in knots only.",
  "_hinweise": {
    "voices": "Each station gets a random voice from pool for each flight. Fixed voices go under stations, e.g. \"EDDF/tower\": \"bf_emma\", \"FIR/EGGX\": \"bm_daniel\", or for a whole station type \"delivery\": \"af_heart\".",
    "airports": "Spoken airport name, climb altitude of the IFR clearance ({initialAlt}), station names that differ from the default and fixed frequencies (\"frequencies\": { \"tower\": \"118.775\" } – these take precedence over the Facilities API).",
    "telephony": "Exceptions and corrections only – all other callsigns come from the OpenFlights database (data/openflights/airlines.dat). An entry here takes precedence.",
    "firs": "FIR (ICAO) → name and frequency of the control unit. Boundaries come from VAT-Spy (data/vatspy), sectors with their own frequencies from the VATSIM sector data (data/sectors); frequency only applies where the sector data has none. oceanic: true = position reports, oceanic clearance beforehand. oceanicFir: identifier of the oceanic unit of a FIR with a domestic and an oceanic part (Gander: CZQX → CZQO). members: further units whose sectors count towards this FIR. Without FIR data in the OFP, the North Atlantic uses EGGX east of 30°W and CZQO west of it. FIRs without an entry of their own are named as in VAT-Spy plus the suffix from firSuffixes (Winnipeg Center), otherwise OCEANIC or CENTER (generic station). There is no VATSIM sector data for KZMP, KZDV and KZLA – their frequencies are those of the MSFS ATC at the FIR boundary in test flight CFG2205.",
    "firSuffixes": "ICAO prefix → station type for FIRs without an entry of their own. The longest matching prefix wins, \"\" for all others.",
    "rules": "Thresholds of the state machine: altitudes in ft, distances in nm, times in seconds or minutes. sectorMinNm: sectors the route touches for a shorter distance don't get a handoff of their own. offerStepClimbs/stepClimbLeadNm: step climbs from the OFP are cleared by ATC on its own (\"when ready climb and maintain …\") this far before the step point. levelRequestUnablePercent: share of level requests answered with \"unable due traffic, expect … in levelRequestDelayMinutes minutes\" (0 = never) – the clearance then follows on its own. checkSquawk/checkFrequency: compare transponder code and COM1 with the assignment; a deviation has to last deviationSeconds (after a handoff frequencyGraceSeconds as well) before ATC says \"check squawk/frequency, should be …\", repeated every deviationRepeatSeconds, at most deviationMaxCalls times. trafficInfo: departure, center and approach call traffic on their own when an aircraft within trafficInfoRangeNm and trafficInfoAltitudeFt will pass within trafficInfoMissNm in the next three minutes (each aircraft once, at most one call a minute). trafficSequencing: on the first call to the tower with traffic ahead on final, the tower gives the sequence (\"number two, follow …\") and clears to land once that aircraft has landed.",
    "words": "Words the state machine inserts for {levelVerb}: climb/descend/maintain in corrections, climbAndMaintain/descendAndMaintain/maintain in level clearances.",
    "messages": "from: atc = Duopilo speaks, pilot = expected pilot call (hint). readback: variables the pilot has to read back.",
    "corrections": "What is said after \"negative\", per readback item."
  },
